# Binary Search — Concept, Template & Nuances

## Prerequisites
- Array must be **sorted**
- Works on any data where you can determine: *"is my answer to the left or right of mid?"*

---

## Why Binary Search?

| n | Linear Search | Binary Search |
|---|---|---|
| 100 | 100 steps | 7 steps |
| 1,000,000 | 1,000,000 steps | 20 steps |
| 1,000,000,000 | 1 billion steps | 30 steps |

**Time: O(log n) | Space: O(1)**

---

## Core Template

```java
int lo = 0, hi = nums.length - 1;

while (lo <= hi) {
    int mid = lo + (hi - lo) / 2;

    if (nums[mid] == target)       return mid;
    else if (nums[mid] < target)   lo = mid + 1;
    else                           hi = mid - 1;
}
return -1;
```

**Why `lo + (hi - lo) / 2`?** Same mid value — but prevents int overflow.
**Why `lo <= hi`?** Handles single element arrays correctly.
**Loop exits when?** `lo > hi` — search space exhausted → return -1.

---

## Nuance 1 — Boundary (First / Last Occurrence)

```java
// First occurrence — on match, keep searching LEFT
if (nums[mid] == target) { result = mid; hi = mid - 1; }

// Last occurrence — on match, keep searching RIGHT
if (nums[mid] == target) { result = mid; lo = mid + 1; }

// Both first + last → two separate passes — O(log n) each
```
> Found target but don't stop — keep shrinking towards the boundary you want.

---

## Nuance 2 — Rotated Array (One Half Always Sorted)

```java
if (nums[lo] <= nums[mid]) {
    // LEFT half sorted
    if (nums[lo] <= target && target < nums[mid]) hi = mid - 1;
    else                                          lo = mid + 1;
} else {
    // RIGHT half sorted
    if (nums[mid] < target && target <= nums[hi]) lo = mid + 1;
    else                                          hi = mid - 1;
}
```

> Use the sorted half to rule out where target isn't — other half is where it must be.

---

## Nuance 3 — Answer Space

```java
int lo = minPossibleAnswer, hi = maxPossibleAnswer, result = -1;

while (lo <= hi) {
    int mid = lo + (hi - lo) / 2;
    if (condition(mid)) { result = mid; hi = mid - 1; } // minimizing
    else                { lo = mid + 1; }
}
return result;
```
> lo/hi are answer boundaries, not indices. Test if mid is a valid answer, shrink the range.

---

## Pattern Summary

| Pattern | Key change from classic |
|---|---|
| Classic | None — base template |
| Boundary | On match: record + keep shrinking |
| Rotated Array | Identify sorted half, use it to eliminate |
| Answer Space | lo/hi are answer range, not indices |
